cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use utu in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: utu
abstract: >-
  utu is a Python library of solar physics utilities built on named-arrays,
  named for the Sumerian god of the sun. Its utilities include the emission
  lines of an optically thin plasma, computed from the CHIANTI atomic
  database, and the differential rotation of the solar surface. Inputs and
  results are named arrays, so they carry physical units and broadcast
  against each other by axis name.
authors:
  - family-names: Smart
    given-names: Roy T.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9997-5515"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sun-data/utu"
url: "https://utu.readthedocs.io"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - solar physics
  - named arrays
